      "report_date": "2026-10-06",
      "title": "Blinder Tunnel Campaign Targets Iraqi Infrastructure",
      "summary": "Iranian state-aligned actor CL-STA-1178 ran the Blinder Tunnel campaign, which targeted Iraqi critical infrastructure in March 2026 after infrastructure staging dating to November 2025. The attackers impersonated Dubai Airports IT recruiters and sent a trojanized Visual Studio coding challenge whose malicious .csproj file executed on project load. The infection chain combined AppDomainManager hijacking, which disabled ETW monitoring, with DLL sideloading to deploy the ShelbyLoader V2 loader, the ShelbyC2 V2 RAT, and the Blackwood Chisel-based tunneling tool. The actors used GitHub's API for command-and-control, including encrypted fallback data hidden in issue comments, to blend traffic with legitimate enterprise activity. Defenders should secure developer environments, monitor anomalous cloud platform traffic, and guard against industry-specific social engineering lures.",
