      "report_date": "2026-10-06",
      "title": "More Shells Than a Seafood Buffet: Tracking Citrix NetScaler Exploitation Activities (CVE-2026-88771)",
      "summary": "Threat actor clusters exploited zero-day vulnerability CVE-2026-88771 in Citrix NetScaler, which Citrix disclosed on September 27, 2026, according to eSentire's Threat Response Unit. Attackers deployed PHP web shells, modified Apache configuration files, and set the SUID bit on /bin/sh to gain root-level access. One pre-disclosure cluster used a lightweight web shell, while a post-disclosure cluster used the Platypus fleet management tool and another created a backdoor NetScaler superuser account. Exploitation occurred within roughly 24 hours of disclosure, and some clusters used watchTowr's public proof-of-concept. Defenders should prioritize patching and monitor for Apache config changes, web shells, /bin/sh permission changes, and NetScaler configuration alterations.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
