      "report_date": "2026-10-06",
      "title": "IronChain Ransomware Threatens Businesses with Permanent Data Loss and Costly Downtime",
      "summary": "IronChain is a PyInstaller-packaged Windows ransomware build, first seen in September 2026, that behaves more like a wiper than a recoverable ransomware. Its RSA private key is discarded, and its encryption mutation state is not preserved, so encrypted files cannot be reliably restored even after payment. A bug in exception handling keeps the main payload reachable, while a separate variable error narrows file traversal. The sample bundles four kernel drivers, but only the Baidu driver forms a coherent process-termination path, and the others are rejected or never called. Defenders should focus on combined indicators such as the SYSTEM scheduled task and driver-service patterns, and maintain tested, isolated backups.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
      "threats": [
        "Ironchain",
        "Deadlock",
        "Byovd_technique"
