      "title": "CITRIX 0-DAY EXPLOITS: CVE-2026–88771 & CVE-2026–88772 IN THE WILD",
      "summary": "Attackers are exploiting two Citrix NetScaler ADC and Gateway zero-days, CVE-2026-88771 and CVE-2026-88772, which are chained to gain root on appliances. CVE-2026-88771 is reached through crafted authentication requests whose strings reach a maintenance script that executes them as root, while CVE-2026-88772 is a UDP/DTLS memory overflow. Post-exploitation tooling creates a rogue superuser, sets SUID on /bin/sh, exfiltrates the nsconfig directory, and deploys password-protected PHP web shells such as WHIPSHOT. The SLAPSHOT Python and Perl tunneler then turns the appliance into an internal pivot point. Defenders should patch to fixed builds immediately and hunt for the described file paths, configuration changes, and rogue accounts.",
